                    <death when="1801-09-09"/>
                    <occupation>classical and biblical scholar</occupation>
                    <occupation>religious controversialist</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin's meetings with Wakefield take place in the homes of <persName key="HOL02">Brand Hollis</persName>, <persName key="FRE01">Frend</persName> (whom Wakefield defended), and
    <persName key="NOR04">Northmore</persName>. He notes Wakefield's death in 1801, although he is a day late  (Wakefield dies 9th Sept). 
    It is unclear to whom later Wakefield entries refer, although his brother Thomas had a parish in Richmond.  There are six later entries, not coded, that appear from 1810 to 1816.</p>
                    </note>
